
# <Navigate /> Component from "react-router-dom"
react-router(v5) - <Redirect />

3 major purposes
****************
1. It's mainly used to redirect from legacy route to a new route.
    if you want /home to be the canonical route for the home component, you can redirect from "/"
    to "/home" using Navigate. 
    <Navigate> is typically used as an element within <Route> or in conditional rendering.

2. Handling conditional redirects, such as authenticated vs. unauthenticated users. (Redirecting users after an event, like form submission or login)
    <Route path="/dashboard" element={isAuthenticated ? <Dashboard /> : <Navigate to="/login" />} />

How many ways to do so
***********************
1. Navigate - more declarative approach
2. useNavigate() hook - imperative approach

# 2. Index Route
Mainly used to render a fallback component when no other route match is provided.
Example: Default Component - Product category (Electronics which may include mobile, cameras, fan, light etc)
Featured & New products are more specific nested routes